      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "HOOK-ANATOMY",
      "narration_text": "A hook is a shell script that runs on a system event — before a file write, before a tool call. The PreToolUse hook receives a JSON payload on stdin describing what Claude is about to do. The script checks the payload. If it detects a grade pattern, it exits with a nonzero code. Claude Code sees that exit code and blocks the write. The file never changes.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
